<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chen Sheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 208 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chen Sheng was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conscription">conscript</a> leader who began the first great rising against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a> in 209 BCE. Delayed by rain and facing execution, he and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-guang">Wu Guang</a> rebelled at Dazexiang, took the city of Chen and proclaimed the state of Zhangchu, reviving the name of Chu. His commanders spread the revolt across the former states, some making themselves kings, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-chen">Wu Chen</a> did in Zhao, before Chen was killed by his own driver in 208 BCE.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The prophecy that even if only three households remained in Chu, it would be Chu that destroyed Qin proved true: in 209 BCE <b>Chen Sheng</b> proclaimed a restored Chu, and two Chu men, Xiang Yan's grandson Xiang Yu and Liu Bang, overthrew the Qin dynasty in 207–206 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/state-of-chu">State of Chu · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Zhang Han was the Qin general who crushed <b>Chen Sheng's</b> rising, then surrendered to Xiang Yu after the defeat of Qin forces at Julu.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-yong">Kingdom of Yong</a></li><li><blockquote>In 209 BCE a party of conscripts led by <b>Chen Sheng</b> and Wu Guang was held up by rain at Dazexiang in Anhui.</blockquote><a href="/state/zhangchu">Zhangchu</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Fangcheng County, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=33.26,113&amp;year=-218" aria-label="Fangcheng County on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7440 956 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Chen Sheng"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7890 1226h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7890 1226h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=33.26,113&amp;year=-218">What was here in 218 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
